@@ -338,3 +338,4 @@ Reserved:
   0193 redesigns App Compatibility (2.0 plan, phase C; owner, 2026-11-12) on the 1.0 Display Compat engine and profile store: each app is Square, Tall phone (720×1440) or Custom (the 1.0 editor), with an App size (100, 85 or 75% of the person's density, only while the app is in front) and a landscape video choice (Fit drops the Tall canvas while the display is sideways, so a 16:9 video fills the width). Out-of-box presets ship as `res/raw/app_compat_presets.tsv` (an image can override it at `/product/etc/sable/app-compat-presets.tsv`): YouTube, Instagram, TikTok and Facebook Tall phone; Google Maps and Android Auto Square. A preset is given once, at install, boot or when the app opens, with a one-line notice, and Reset brings it back. New list and one-app page, 29 new strings in all 19 languages, `AppCompatTest`. Crop to fill and Hold Space come later with a framework patch.
   0194 adds **Older code loading** to App Compatibility's one-app page (owner, 2026-11-12): it adds or removes the app in `persist.sys.sable.legacy_dcl`, the list frameworks/base 0328 reads to let an app load code it wrote itself (Pluto TV's ad library), then stops the app so its next start uses it. `CodeLoading` matches the framework's default list (`tv.pluto.android`) and the 91-character property limit; 4 new strings in all 19 languages.
   0195 adds Sable presets for Tubi (`com.tubitv`), Google TV (`com.google.android.videos`) and YouTube Music (`com.google.android.apps.youtube.music`): Tall phone with landscape video Fit, like YouTube and Instagram (owner's videos, 2026-11-12). The shipped-presets test now also checks Fit.
+  0196 drops the home's Permissions page as well (owner, 2026-11-12): SableHomeAccess already grants them, so Launcher settings and first-run setup open on Appearance & Home, the steps renumber 1-5, the Review page loses its Permissions card, and the Next/Back footer (`Settings2Flow`) no longer walks into the removed Permissions or Active Frames pages. The Weather hint points to Android Settings > Apps for location; `home_access` checks it.
